{"_id":"68a736138ec3d8323af14d59","nodeId":"W6RnhoD7fW2xzVwnyJEDr","roadmapSlug":"data-engineer","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:58.672Z","description":"# Graph\n\nGraph databases store data as nodes and edges, representing entities and the relationships between them. They are optimized for queries that traverse relationships, such as finding connections between users or mapping dependencies. Graph databases are used in social networks, fraud detection, recommendation engines, and knowledge graphs.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"What is a Graph database?","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/nosql/graph/","_id":"6a7f4a42cb44947debcf5207"},{"type":"article","title":"Graph database","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graph_database","_id":"6a7f4a42cb44947debcf5208"},{"type":"video","title":"Introduction to NoSQL","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qI_g07C_Q5I","_id":"6a7f4a42cb44947debcf5209"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:02:58.294Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04e1fb5fcb94d0417044","title":"DataCamp - Associate Data Engineer in SQL","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/WOP6XG"},{"_id":"6a5e04e1fb5fcb94d0417100","title":"DataCamp - Data Engineer in Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/JkYLbr"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/data-engineer/content/W6RnhoD7fW2xzVwnyJEDr.md"}